  "legacyHoldReasons": {
    "f_654az5cs4ya2c": "DBIA171 (p.34) compares Tamil cūci/ūci, Malayalam sūci/tūśi, Kannada sūci/sūji/sūje, Telugu sūdi and other Dravidian needle forms with Sanskrit sūc-, Prakrit sui- and Hindi sui/sūji. The selected survey forms require source-local borrowing-route evidence, not automatic inherited links or a jump to Sanskrit. The current DBIA Indo-Aryan node is incorrectly headed cūcub (the Parji comparator in the OCR); it is not a usable donor.",
    "f_jcjkrbqvfoq36": "DBIA318(p.58) treats Kannada baṭṭe, Kodagu batte, Tulu baṭṭe, Telugu baṭṭa and Kota bat as loans ultimately from Sanskrit paṭṭa cloth, explicitly rejecting derivation from vastra. The selected survey forms need an immediate-donor/transmission analysis; do not label them inherited or automatically jump to Sanskrit. Compound/paired responses also require constituent analysis.",
    "f_4w6r5qbezpcpw": "DBIA318(p.58) treats Kannada baṭṭe, Kodagu batte, Tulu baṭṭe, Telugu baṭṭa and Kota bat as loans ultimately from Sanskrit paṭṭa cloth, explicitly rejecting derivation from vastra. The selected survey forms need an immediate-donor/transmission analysis; do not label them inherited or automatically jump to Sanskrit. Compound/paired responses also require constituent analysis.",
    "f_eovfhnf5ukm6o": "The full DEDR appendix57 places Tamil/Malayalam vāl, Kannada bāla, Kota vālm, Kodagu bālï and Telugu vālamu alongside CDIAL11572 vāla-/vāra-. The existing appendix parent f_wqel4vcg76coc has an empty Form label. Do not attach these survey responses to an unnamed parent or skip to a remote Sanskrit ancestor before the historical route and immediate donor/parent are resolved.",
    "f_yct2lzwqlmjhk": "The full DEDR appendix57 places Tamil/Malayalam vāl, Kannada bāla, Kota vālm, Kodagu bālï and Telugu vālamu alongside CDIAL11572 vāla-/vāra-. The existing appendix parent f_wqel4vcg76coc has an empty Form label. Do not attach these survey responses to an unnamed parent or skip to a remote Sanskrit ancestor before the historical route and immediate donor/parent are resolved.",
    "f_3atfaami555x2": "DEDR3283 expressly lists dūḷi/dhūli-type dust terms in several Dravidian languages as direct Sanskrit dhūli loans, and notes contact influence in related dūḷ/dūḷu forms. These survey responses require a supported immediate route/donor; do not label them unqualified inherited reflexes from the dictionary grouping.",
    "f_3sglr6k46elwu": "DEDR3283 expressly lists dūḷi/dhūli-type dust terms in several Dravidian languages as direct Sanskrit dhūli loans, and notes contact influence in related dūḷ/dūḷu forms. These survey responses require a supported immediate route/donor; do not label them unqualified inherited reflexes from the dictionary grouping.",
    "f_s43zaqkywk74k": "DEDR2272 gives Kannada cakkaḷa skin/leather beside Tamil cakkili, a leather-working community name; the existing parent is labelled cakkili. Survey cakaḷu/cakḷu/sekḷa needs a resolved skin-stem parent and historical relation before using that occupational-name head as an ancestor.",
    "f_6nsdezu7gj7ee": "DEDR2272 gives Kannada cakkaḷa skin/leather beside Tamil cakkili, a leather-working community name; the existing parent is labelled cakkili. Survey cakaḷu/cakḷu/sekḷa needs a resolved skin-stem parent and historical relation before using that occupational-name head as an ancestor.",
    "f_u3wajuatex5bg": "Full DBIA233(a) gives Tamil pakkam, Malayalam pakkam/pakkal, Kannada pakka and Telugu pakka side/near, deriving the family from Sanskrit pakṣa- and Prakrit pakkha-. The survey form is a strong lexical match, but the immediate borrowing route for this particular language is not established; do not encode an inherited Dravidian reflex or silently choose Sanskrit over a regional intermediary.",
    "f_ywpgbmkap4vlq": "Full DEDR50 labels this kin-term family probably from Indo-Aryan ārya-/ajja-, and notes independent borrowing for Kurux. The survey match is strong, but an inherited reflex would erase that diagnosis; establish a concrete donor/route before assigning. Older-brother versus father/grandfather usage also needs source-specific checking.",
    "f_ruc4d6aadxasq": "Full DEDR50 labels this kin-term family probably from Indo-Aryan ārya-/ajja-, and notes independent borrowing for Kurux. The survey match is strong, but an inherited reflex would erase that diagnosis; establish a concrete donor/route before assigning. Older-brother versus father/grandfather usage also needs source-specific checking.",
    "f_qrvby2rilkf2g": "DBIA97 derives Tamil kālam/kālai time and Kodagu kāla year from Sanskrit kāla. Survey morning/year forms retain that lexical family, but their immediate borrowing history is not established; do not silently label them inherited or skip to remote Sanskrit."
  }
